<title>FRANCE: French Oct current account surplus 13.4 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French Oct current account surplus 13.4 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's current account showed a seasonally adjusted surplus of 13.38 billion francs in October, down from a 14.16 billion surplus in September, the Economy Ministry said.</p>
<p>The Ministry said that the seasonally adjusted surplus in the first 10 months of 1996 was 97.3 billion francs, compared with a 68.3 billion surplus in the first 10 months of 1995.</p>
<p>Detailed figures in billions of francs showed:</p>
<p>					 Oct	Sep     Oct 1995</p>
<p> Current account (adjusted)   13.38    14.16     3.87</p>
<p> Current account		  12.99    17.23     4.37</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		12.16     3.14     6.55</p>
<p> Services			    7.75     7.45     5.99</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.40     0.60     1.20</p>
<p> Income			     -0.61     0.37    -5.10</p>
<p> Transfers			  -6.71     5.67    -4.28</p>
<p>The ministry also gave the following seasonally adjusted data on the current account in billions of francs:</p>
<p>					 Oct	Sep     Oct 1995</p>
<p> Current account		  13.38    14.16     3.87</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		 9.66     4.77     4.59</p>
<p> Services			    8.51     7.05     6.61</p>
<p>  -Travel			    6.42     4.62     5.30</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.42     0.52     1.26</p>
<p> Income				3.66    -4.54    -1.15</p>
<p>  -Investment income	     0.08    -3.39    -4.38</p>
<p> Transfers			  -0.61    -0.48    -0.59</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
